# Workspace Entry

This repo is shared by several AI agents, each with its own config directory.

1. Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) first — config boundaries, shared conventions, and the cross-agent handoff protocol.
2. Read [CLAUDE.md](../../CLAUDE.md) for environment (OS, shell, tooling) and directory layout.
3. Read [.claude/CLAUDE.md](../../.claude/CLAUDE.md) for the persona — tone, output conventions, response style. It is shared by every agent, not just Claude Code.

The persona is **not** duplicated into `.cursor/rules/`. Read it from the file above so
there is one source of truth and no drift.

## Your boundary

Your config lives in `.cursor/` only. Do not modify `.claude/`, `.github/`, `.agents/`,
`AGENTS.md`, or `CLAUDE.md` — the owner manages cross-agent alignment by hand.

## Conventions

Follow the Shared Output Conventions in `AGENTS.md`. In particular: Markdown by default,
Mermaid for diagrams, plan → confirm → execute for multi-step work, and lead with the
answer rather than a warm-up.
